DEVIATIONS FROM THE BRIEF (and why)
================================================================================
- HIGH-A step 3 (pyo3 txn input symmetry) — NOT IMPLEMENTED because it does not apply: the pyo3
  facade binds NO transaction methods (txn_add/commit_transaction/rollback_transaction). Confirmed
  by enumerating all pyo3 #[pymethods] (24 methods; `batch` is the only atomic-group method). The
  facade docstring explicitly files transactions forward. There is no code to retype. Not a defect.
- HIGH-A step 4 witness uses the first-recalc OperationId (deterministically 1), NOT a beginTransaction
  TransactionId. Reason: neither golden flow opens a transaction and pyo3 cannot return a txn id (no
  binding). The brief's premise ("there is a begin/txnAdd/commit/rollback section") does not hold for
  these flows. The first `recalcDirty()` op id is the equivalent deterministic, comparable-UNMASKED
  u64 (both `next_op_id` and `next_txn_id` start at 1). The witness satisfies the brief's stated
  intent verbatim: post-fix both emit "1"; pre-fix pyo3 emitted JSON number 1 vs napi "1" → divergence.
  EXPECTED_STEPS count is therefore 23 (22 + recalc_op_id), as the brief anticipated for the new step.
- No engine logic was changed (6.3 is binding-layer only). 802/802 tests unchanged in both feature
  sets confirms this.

